{"study_accession":"PRJNA686671","secondary_study_accession":"SRP298577","title":"Next Generation Sequencing Facilitates Quantitative Analysis of Osteoarthritis related long non-coding RNAs (LcnRNAs)","description":"Purpose: LncRNAs are important moleculars in immune responses. The goals of this study are to identify osteoarthritis related lncRNAs. Methods: PBMCs from healthy control and osteoarthritis patients were collected. Then, the next-generation libraries of mRNA were prepared using VAHTS mRNA-seq v2 Library Prep Kit for Illumina® (Vazyme, Nanjing, China). The Library quality was determined by Bioanalyzer 4200 (Agilent, Santa Clara, CA, USA). Then the mRNA-seq libraries were sequenced in HiSeq ⅹ10 system (Illumina, San Diego, CA, USA) on a 150bp paired-end run. The differentially expressed lncRNAs were selected as having more than 1 fold difference in their geometrical mean expression between the compared groups and a statistically significant p-value (<0.05) by analysis of DEseq2. The GO analysis on differentially expressed lncRNAs was performed with an R package: Clusterprofiler using a p<0.05 to define statistically enriched GO categories. Results: 18 lncRNAs decreased significantly in osteoarthritis patients. Overall design: LncRNA profiles of PBMC from healthy controls and osteoarthritis patients were generated by deep sequencing, in triplicate, using illumina HiSeq ⅹ10 system","pubmed":"33519887","geo_series":"","n_samples":6,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17120537","study_accession":"PRJNA686671","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PBMCs, Osteoarthritis rep1","description":"PBMCs, Osteoarthritis rep1","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM4981616","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-02-10","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["cell_type","Peripheral blood mononuclear cell"],["disease","Osteoarthritis patients"],["sex","female"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13276976","experiment_accession":"SRX9706778","library_l